      "side": 1,
      "message": "Two CSS styling issues here:\n\n1. **Specificity of `del code` / `ins code` when nested inside links or emphasis**: `.diff-cell.modified-right :not(pre):not(del):not(ins) \u003e code` (lines 373–380) has specificity `(0, 5, 1)`, which beats `del code` and `ins code` `(0, 0, 2)`. When an inline `\u003ccode\u003e` span is nested inside a link or bold/italic inside `\u003cdel\u003e` or `\u003cins\u003e` (e.g. `\u003cins class\u003d\"diff-highlight-add\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"...\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e--flag\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/ins\u003e` or `\u003cdel class\u003d\"diff-highlight-del\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003e--flag\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/del\u003e`), the direct parent of `\u003ccode\u003e` is `\u003ca\u003e` or `\u003cstrong\u003e` (which matches `:not(pre):not(del):not(ins)`), so the code span receives the gray `--disabled-background` instead of the red/green `del code` / `ins code` highlight.\n2. **Unused classes `.diff-list-item-*` and `.diff-table-row-*`**: `markdown-diff-util.ts` emits `class\u003d\"diff-list-item-del\"`, `class\u003d\"diff-list-item-add\"`, `class\u003d\"diff-table-row-del\"`, and `class\u003d\"diff-table-row-add\"`, but there are no corresponding styles in `gr-diff-markdown-viewer.ts` (so empty cells in added/deleted table rows have no highlight).\n\n_from potto_",
