      "side": 1,
      "message": "`getContainerDelimiters` returns asymmetric delimiters on combined bold+italic tokens (`***...***` or `___...___`).\n\nWhen `Lexer.lexInline(\u0027***bold italic***\u0027)` parses triple asterisks/underscores, the outer `em` token has `token.raw \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027***bold italic***\u0027` and its child `strong` token has `innerRaw \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027**bold italic**\u0027`. Because `innerRaw` starts with `*`, `token.raw.indexOf(innerRaw)` matches at `idx \u003d 0` instead of `idx \u003d 1`, returning `openDelim: \u0027\u0027` and `closeDelim: \u0027**\u0027`. As a result:\n- `tokenizeWords(\u0027***bold italic***\u0027)` emits `[\u0027**\u0027, \u0027bold\u0027, \u0027 \u0027, \u0027italic\u0027, \u0027**\u0027, \u0027**\u0027]` (4 trailing asterisks, so `pos` in `renderSideInlineDiff` becomes misaligned with `fullText`).\n- `innerStart` in `renderTokensWithDiffRanges` (line 764) is off by 1 character.\n\nSince container tokens (`em`, `strong`, `del`) have symmetric delimiters around `innerRaw`, computing the delimiter length via `const idx \u003d (token.raw.length - innerRaw.length) / 2` (when `idx \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 token.raw.slice(idx, idx + innerRaw.length) \u003d\u003d\u003d innerRaw`) avoids matching part of the outer delimiter.\n\n_from potto_",
