      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T23:11:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Handle `token.type \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027escape\u0027` in `renderInlineAstTokens` so backslash escapes do not render literal backslashes.\n\nWhen Marked lexes backslash-escaped characters (e.g. `\\*`, `\\[`, `\\|`, `\\\\`), it emits an `escape` token with `raw: \u0027\\\\*\u0027` and `text: \u0027*\u0027`. Falling through to `parts.push(token.raw)` renders the literal backslash in the DOM (regression from `marked.parse()` before this change). Handling `token.type \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027escape\u0027` with `parts.push((token as Tokens.Escape).text)` renders the unescaped character.\n\n_from potto_",
