      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T23:11:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`contentA` and `contentB` filter out whitespace (`!/^\\s+$/.test(t)`) but retain punctuation tokens (such as `.`, `,`, `|`). Because `overlapDistance` (`1 - commonCount / Math.min(contentA.length, contentB.length)`) has no length-ratio guard and is always `\u003c\u003d diceDistance`:\n\n- Any short sentence (e.g. 3–4 words ending in `.`) compared against a long, unrelated paragraph that shares a single stop word (e.g. `is` or `the`) plus a period `.` will have `commonCount \u003e\u003d 2` and `overlapDistance \u003c\u003d 0.6`, triggering a noisy word-level diff instead of a full block replacement.\n- In `renderTableDiff` (line 1143), joining cells with `\u0027 | \u0027` injects `N - 1` pipe (`\u0027|\u0027`) tokens into every row in an `N`-column table. In a 3+ column table, any two rows automatically share `\u003e\u003d 2` pipe tokens (`commonCount \u003e\u003d 2`), causing completely disjoint rows with short cells to get `overlapDistance \u003c\u003d 0.6` and be paired as `\u0027modified\u0027`.\n\nConsider excluding pure-punctuation tokens when computing `contentA`/`contentB`, bounding the length ratio for `overlapDistance`, and joining table cells with whitespace (`\u0027 \u0027`) in `renderTableDiff`.\n\n_from potto_",
