      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T23:11:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A few structural edge cases in `renderListDiff` and `renderBlockquoteDiff`:\n\n1. **Nested lists**: `item.text` in Marked includes the raw markdown of any nested sublist (e.g. `- Parent\\n  - Child`). Passing `item.text` to `renderInlineMarkdown` / `renderInlineTextDiff` (which use `Lexer.lexInline`) flattens nested lists onto a single line as literal text instead of rendering nested `\u003cul\u003e`/`\u003col\u003e` elements.\n2. **Ordered list start index**: If an `\u003col\u003e` starts at an index other than 1 (`tokenA.start` / `tokenB.start`), the `\u003col\u003e` tag here (and in `renderTokenToHtml` at line 670) omits the `start` attribute.\n3. **Multi-paragraph / structured blockquotes**: In `renderBlockquoteDiff` (line 1072), passing `tokenA.text.trim()` into `renderInlineTextDiff(..., \u0027p\u0027)` collapses multi-paragraph blockquotes (`\u003e para 1\\n\u003e\\n\u003e para 2`) or blockquotes containing lists/code blocks into a single `\u003cp\u003e` element.\n\n_from potto_",
