      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T23:11:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `uA \u003d\u003d\u003d uB \u003e 1`, returning a positive fallback score (`0.01 + 0.1 * (1 - dist)`) for all `(a, b)` pairs of matching `type` even when `dist \u003e DEFAULT_MAX_HOMOLOGOUS_DISTANCE` can misalign blocks across insertions/deletions.\n\nFor example, if an interval has 2 blocks on each side where `A[0]` was deleted, `A[1]` was modified into `B[0]`, and an unrelated `B[1]` was added:\n- If `A[0]` and `B[1]` have the same type (e.g. `paragraph`) and `A[1]`/`B[0]` have a different type (e.g. `code` with `dist \u003e 0.6`), DP can pair `A[0]` with `B[1]`.\n\nIf the fallback is only intended to keep a single replaced block side-by-side in one row, consider restricting it to `uA \u003d\u003d\u003d 1 \u0026\u0026 uB \u003d\u003d\u003d 1`.\n\n_from potto_",
